title: "DeepRootGen: A stochastic framework for three-dimensional root system architecture simulation and reconstruction"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: GPL-3.0
url: "https://github.com/Plant-Food-Research-Open/deep-root-gen"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Plant-Food-Research-Open/deep-root-gen"
keywords:
  - root system architecture
  - root simulation
  - woody perennials
  - stochastic simulation
  - three-dimensional modelling
  - model calibration
  - sensitivity analysis
  - simulation-based inference
abstract: >
  DeepRootGen is a stochastic simulation framework for generating, analysing,
  and digitally reconstructing three-dimensional plant root system architectures.
  Root systems are represented as hierarchical graphs of root organs and segments,
  supporting analysis of branching patterns, morphology, spatial extent, and root
  length density. The framework supports parameter calibration, sensitivity
  analysis, and comparisons between simulated architectures and field observations.
